-- title:
--   Membership in the component comp₀ via vanishing q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\neq 0$ with $p\mid M$, a subgroup $H\leq(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and the hypothesis $hj$ that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` (namely $q^{-1}$ times the power series `jNum` with coefficients pushed to $\mathbb{Q}$) lies in the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}(\text{intFormRatiosC})\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ attached to $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{P}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, i.e. a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model over $R_p=\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ of the curve with $q$-expansion function field at level $\Gamma_H(M)$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa=\kappa_A$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$; let $\rho\colon R_p\to A$ be a ring map compatible with the structure map $R_p\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $\kappa$ an $R_p$-algebra via the residue map composed with $\rho$. Let $\mathcal{O}_\infty=$ `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj` be the pole-chart algebra, i.e. the subalgebra `chartAlg` of the function field attached to the single element $(jAt)^{-1}$, and let $\mathrm{red}\colon\mathcal{O}_\infty\to\kappa((q))$ be a ring homomorphism such that, whenever $y\in R_p((q))$ has image in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ equal to the $q$-expansion of $b\in\mathcal{O}_\infty$, one has $\mathrm{red}(b)$ equal to the coefficientwise image of $y$ under $\kappa\leftarrow A\leftarrow R_p$. Let $c'\colon\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa\otimes_{R_p}\mathcal{O}_\infty)\to$ `fibre` $=\mathrm{pullback}$ of the structure morphism along $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, be a morphism whose first projection is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight` followed by the pole-chart immersion $\iota_\infty$, and whose second projection is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom`. Then for every point $z$ of $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa\otimes_{R_p}\mathcal{O}_\infty)$, the image $c'(z)$ lies in the set-theoretic range of the underlying map of the morphism $\mathfrak{P}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,h_A\,\rho\,h_\rho\,0$ if and only if the ideal generated by the image of $\ker(\mathrm{red})$ under `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight` is contained in the prime ideal $z$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion principle in chart form: on the pole chart of the special fibre at a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$, the component indexed by $0$ in the model data — the component through the cusp $\infty$ — is cut out exactly by those functions whose $q$-expansion reduces to zero, so that membership of a point in that component becomes the inclusion of the ideal generated by $\ker(\mathrm{red})$. It is used in the identification of the minimal primes of the pole chart of the special fibre, in the comparison of ideal-theoretic criteria for lying on the component, and in the compatibility of the component morphisms with base twists.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_mem_range_comp_zero_iff_map_ker_le.lean

